  "findings": [
    "R4D compiled Zig helper support was added through the canonical SDK manifest/build path; native driver fixture compiles the same bounded parser as DISPLAYD.",
    "Existing 55U8K upstream fixture contains an invalid 420 bitmap index. Raw extension is rejected; only a test-local repaired copy exercises the valid audio branch.",
    "Descriptor range-offset bits in EDID1.4 are recognized as metadata, not reserved zero padding. Established/standard timing identities remain nominal until a complete timing is available.",
    "Shared PS7 build forwards an explicit argument array so Zig flags cannot be bound as PowerShell parameter names; --help and actual owner builds succeed.",
    "R4DESK must start as the system shell. Its existing window-idle smoke additionally needs AppDefaults and MemView; a private canonical catalog adds exactly those Full modules to regular Test.",
    "Private catalog first derives baseline Test plus explicit extras, then adds only missing regular Test includes to stay inside the existing bounded include list."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Only the generic commit/rollback model and firmware retain no-op are implemented. Native GPU callbacks, scanout BO leases, physical mode programming and coordinated surface geometry transitions remain future driver work.",
    "Test-only observes current BO/fence state without reservations. A later native commit must revalidate and acquire actual leases/admission under the shared display execution owner.",
    "EDID decoding covers bounded base, CTA and DisplayID type I/VII. Unsupported metadata, CVT/GTF synthesis, DSC, VRR and complete HDR policy are explicitly unknown/unimplemented.",
    "Firmware data is a boot snapshot, not live cable status. Missing actual Hisense extension proves no HDMI audio capability.",
    "Acceptance images were assembled before release publication and may report release0.79.6; the tested kernel/module artifacts are the final 0.79.7 source artifacts bound here.",
    "Debian execution tested; Windows PS7 path shares logic but was not executed."
  ],
  "reproduce": "Restore saved PS7 helpers under Temp/gfx-07907; build Kernel, SDK, Example, DisplayDiag, Desktop, AppDefaults and MemView via owner starters. Run Run-Qemu.ps1 native, software and desktop sequentially with fresh private media and four vCPUs. Test AUTOEXEC is restored byte-for-byte."
}
